course: dictionary
lesson: 4232
title: Grandad, a family word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Grandad is a friendly word for your grandfather, the father of your mum or dad. Most people have two grandads, one on each side of the family.
explain: You can also use Grandad as a name when you talk to him, with a capital G: «Hi, Grandad!» Here Grandad is not a description, it is how you call him.
explain: Read the words around it to be sure. «Afterwards Grandad may go quiet and busy himself on the farm» tells you Grandad is a person in the family, because he has his own way of coping and is part of the story.
fact: Grandad means your grandfather, your mum's or dad's father.
fact: «Hi, Grandad!» shows that Grandad can also be the name you call him.
fact: Other words with the same meaning are grandpa, granddad, grandfather, gramps and pop.
fact: Most people have two grandads, one from each side of the family.
fact: A grandad is two generations above you in a family tree.
exercise: Who is a grandad? | Your mum's or dad's brother | Your teacher at school | *Your mum's or dad's father | A friend from your class
exercise: «Grandad watched his match videos on her phone and was proud.» Who watched the match videos? | Jamie | *Grandad | Oscar | Mum
exercise: When you say «Hi, Grandad!», what is Grandad? | A kind of bird | A place you visit at weekends | A food you eat at tea | *The name you call him
test: Which word also means grandfather? | Cousin | *Gramps | Teacher | Puppy
test: How many grandads do most people have? | Three | Four | *Two | One
exam: In a family tree at school, where is a grandad? | Under you, one generation below | On the same level as your brother | *Two generations above you | Not in the tree at all
